 src/cleanup/Makefile.in                   |  9 +++++++-
 src/cleanup/cleanup_milter.c              | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/cleanup/cleanup_milter_dsn_origin.in  |  3 +++
 src/cleanup/cleanup_milter_dsn_origin.ref |  6 +++++
 5 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/cleanup/cleanup_milter_dsn_origin.in
 create mode 100644 src/cleanup/cleanup_milter_dsn_origin.ref

diff --git a/proto/MILTER_README.html b/proto/MILTER_README.html
index c8a557767..2619b59e4 100644
--- a/proto/MILTER_README.html
+++ b/proto/MILTER_README.html
@@ -469,6 +469,32 @@ or body_checks (lines 3-5 below).  </p>
 </pre>
 </blockquote>
 
+<h4> Delivery status notification origin </h4>
+
+<p> A Milter cannot determine from message content whether a delivery
+status notification was generated by the local Postfix MTA.  Postfix
+therefore provides the following macro: </p>
+
+<dl compact>
+
+<dt> <tt>{postfix_dsn_origin}</tt> </dt> <dd> The value is <tt>internal</tt>
+for a null-sender delivery status notification posted by bounce(8), and
+<tt>external</tt> otherwise.  The latter includes delivery status
+notifications received from outside Postfix and other internally-generated
+mail. </dd>
+
+</dl>
+
+<p> A Milter can request this macro name through normal Milter macro-list
+negotiation.  Otherwise, specify the name in an appropriate Postfix Milter
+macro parameter such as milter_end_of_header_macros.  Milters that do not
+request the name are unaffected. </p>
+
+<p> The <tt>internal</tt> value identifies the Postfix origin of a delivery
+status notification.  A Milter is still responsible for validating the
+null sender, the delivery status notification structure and content, and
+any embedded message. </p>
+
 <h3><a name="errors">Milter error handling</a></h3>
 
 <p> The milter_default_action parameter specifies how Postfix handles
